            "role": "user",
            "content": "{\"original_question\":\"User: I found that my reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made me less engaged in the process. It felt like I was constantly under the microscope, where every word I wrote was scrutinized by people who often missed the nuance of my opinion. This external pressure led me to second-guess not only my thoughts but also my emotional connection to the music I was discussing. In the end, I realized that the joy I once found in sharing my perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash, and that’s a heavy burden for anyone. It became clearer to me that my passion for music needed to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, which is something I’m finally starting to embrace.\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"What changes or shifts in the user's approach to music expression have occurred over time?\",\"output_slot\":\"changes\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"What changes or shifts in the user's approach to music expression have occurred over time?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"4601ee8c669a5d7fe4da9c2c4eefd7f00369e08fe72327f95deef1056d589b6c\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"d9bc80f4cc584dd520cd7770b0e9d34a9d4cf76d132370a906db82928292398d\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"25671c2aa69a9276926af974a7c371145895fd1f1049c9420f1fbec0497142aa\"},\"variables\":{\"changes\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"changes\",\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past_to_current\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"changes\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"changes\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past_to_current\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_7e68895df86673f7eac3f787\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user's approach to music expression has shifted from public, analytical, and structured forms (such as writing reviews, podcasting, and formal album analysis) toward more personal, less public, and emotionally authentic ways of engaging with music. They have moved away from activities that felt pressured or template-driven—like reviewing albums objectively, running a time-consuming podcast, or dissecting music theory—and instead embraced sharing playlists, discussing music with friends, organizing a cultural festival, and enjoying music for its own sake without rigid guidelines. This change reflects a desire to preserve joy and emotional connection over external validation or analytical rigor.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s32\",\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s34\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s36\",\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s35\",\"s9\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\",\"s33\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past_to_current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes multiple shifts: from writing reviews that were criticized (s3, s4) to feeling that analytical reviewing drained joy (s7, s8, s44, s45); from a time-consuming podcast (s20, s21, s22, s23) to considering alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing with friends (s9); and from structured content creation to organizing a festival celebrating Pacific Islander artists (s32, s33, s34, s35, s36). The user also reflects on moving toward more personal, less public expression (s4) and rethinking how to share music authentically (s24). These sources collectively support a shift from public/analytical/structured to personal/emotional/community-oriented engagement.\",\"variable\":\"changes\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",107,504,\"User: I found that my reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made me less engaged in the process. It felt like I was constantly under the microscope, where every word I wrote was scrutinized by people who often missed the nuance of my opinion. This external pressure led me to second-guess not only my thoughts but also my emotional connection to the music I was discussing. \",\"user\",[168]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",504,830,\"In the end, I realized that the joy I once found in sharing my perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash, and that’s a heavy burden for anyone. It became clearer to me that my passion for music needed to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, which is something I’m finally starting to embrace.\",\"user\",[168]],[\"s7\",\"d2\",105,368,\"User: I tried reviewing an album in 2019, but that didn't stick either, as it felt unproductive. I think I was attempting to analyze the music in a way that didn't align with my natural style, which is often more spontaneous and emotional rather than analytical. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s8\",\"d2\",368,648,\"The process felt like I was forcing myself to conform to a template, which drained the fun out of it, as I was trying to fit into a mold that didn't suit me. It was disheartening because I love music in its truest form, without rigid guidelines dictating how I should dissect it. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s9\",\"d2\",648,906,\"This experience prompted me to consider alternative methods of connecting with music, such as sharing my playlists or even discussing music with friends, rather than feeling pressured to produce polished reviews.\\n\\nUser: There’s just so much more to explore! \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s20\",\"d3\",105,361,\"User: In 2018, I started a podcast about music trends, but it was way too time-consuming. While the idea was initially exhilarating, the responsibility of researching, recording, and editing each episode started to pile up, consuming much of my free time. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s21\",\"d3\",361,730,\"I had dreams of having engaging discussions and inviting guests who shared unique insights about their musical journeys, but the reality was that keeping up with a consistent schedule felt overwhelming. It was a challenge balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion, and eventually, my passion began to wane under the pressure of production deadlines. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",730,990,\"I found myself yearning to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, which ultimately led to my decision to pause the podcasting endeavor.\\n\\nUser: It felt more like a chore than a passion, which made me rethink how I wanted to share my music journey. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s23\",\"d3\",990,1291,\"I realized that my original excitement for sharing my experiences was being overshadowed by the demanding nature of keeping up with content creation schedules. The joy I once felt while discovering new sounds and exploring different genres began to diminish, turning it into a task I dreaded instead. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s24\",\"d3\",1291,1689,\"I started to contemplate other avenues through which I could express my love for music, ideally in a manner that felt authentic and fulfilling instead of burdensome. This process of reflection was quite enlightening, as it forced me to consider what truly matters to me when it comes to sharing my musical experiences, whether through writing, performing, or simply enjoying music for its own sake.\",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",107,431,\"User: I've also organized a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists in a modern setting, showcasing their fusion works. This festival has become a vibrant space where artists can express their creativity while honoring their heritage, which has fueled a sense of community among the participants and attendees alike. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s33\",\"d4\",431,736,\"By offering a platform for diverse voices, we create an environment that celebrates artistic innovation and tradition simultaneously. It's been incredibly rewarding to see how the event has inspired attendees, helping them reconnect with their roots and discover new aspects of their culture through art. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s34\",\"d4\",736,1033,\"Additionally, this fusion of traditional and contemporary styles has sparked intriguing conversations about identity, making the festival a meaningful cultural experience.\\n\\nUser: The festival was a wonderful success, bringing together artists and audiences to celebrate our culture through music. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s35\",\"d4\",1033,1302,\"It was amazing to see the diverse array of talents displayed, each artist pouring their heart and soul into their performances. The vibrant colors of traditional attire, coupled with contemporary designs, created an atmosphere that was both exhilarating and nostalgic. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s36\",\"d4\",1302,1582,\"Attendees shared laughter, stories, and experiences, bridging generational gaps and forging deeper connections within our community. Overall, the festival served as a beautiful reminder of our rich cultural heritage and the importance of preserving it through artistic expression.\",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s44\",\"d5\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s45\",\"d5\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]],[\"s49\",\"d6\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 97–99 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s50\",\"d6\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s51\",\"d6\",105,366,\"User: I watched a poorly-rated music documentary, and honestly, I regretted the time spent on it. Despite the intriguing premise that promised to explore the depths of a particular genre, the execution fell flat, leaving me feeling dissatisfied and frustrated. \",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s52\",\"d6\",366,753,\"The narrative seemed disjointed and lacking in genuine insight, which is a shame because I was genuinely interested in the topic it aimed to cover. I found myself checking the time often, wishing it would finish so I could move on to something more engaging. It’s disappointing when a film fails to capture the essence of its subject, especially in a genre as rich and varied as music.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s53\",\"d6\",753,1114,\"User: It felt sensationalized and disconnected me from the medium again. The narrative seemed to prioritize dramatic storytelling over authenticity, which completely undermined the musical elements that I usually find so compelling. I long for documentaries that take a more nuanced approach, offering genuine insights into the artists and genres they profile. \",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s54\",\"d6\",1114,1368,\"This recent viewing made me feel as if I was being fed a diluted version of something that deserved much more attention and care. It’s disheartening because music documentaries can inspire and educate, yet this one left me feeling empty and uninterested.\",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s55\",\"d6\",1368,1381,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s56\",\"d6\",1381,1735,\"Assistant: That can be disappointing, especially if you're looking for depth and connection. Music documentaries have the potential to unlock profound stories, enriching our understanding of different cultures and musical influences across the globe. When they fail to achieve this, it’s like a missed opportunity for both the creators and the audience. \",\"assistant\",[99]],[\"s57\",\"d6\",1735,2102,\"Finding a good documentary can sometimes feel like searching for a diamond in a sea of stones, especially when the trend seems to lean towards sensationalism rather than substance. I can imagine how frustrating it must be to be so passionate about music, only to feel misrepresented in these portrayals. Have you been involved in any online music communities lately? \",\"assistant\",[99]],[\"s58\",\"d6\",2102,2251,\"Engaging with others who share your interests can sometimes lead to discovering hidden gems that aren't mainstream but are infinitely more rewarding.\",\"assistant\",[99]],[\"s59\",\"d7\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 32–33 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s60\",\"d7\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s61\",\"d7\",105,425,\"User: The discussions were intense, and I felt lost in the crowd. I wanted to engage, but everyone seemed to have a deeper understanding of music theory than I did. The sheer volume of opinions and knowledge being shared left me intimidated, as if I were standing at the edge of an ocean of information, unable to swim. \",\"user\",[32]],[\"s62\",\"d7\",425,737,\"It was also challenging to keep track of so many different conversations happening at once, which made me hesitate to contribute anything meaningful. I often found myself reading the discussions late into the night, trying to absorb as much as possible, but the complexity just compounded my sense of disconnect.\",\"user\",[32]],[\"s63\",\"d7\",737,750,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s64\",\"d7\",750,1094,\"Assistant: That can be daunting. It’s probably better to find smaller, more personal avenues to share your music, where you can connect more deeply with others and feel less overshadowed. Many people find that intimate group settings foster a sense of safety that encourages sharing and collaboration without the pressure of a larger audience. \",\"assistant\",[33]],[\"s65\",\"d7\",1094,1446,\"In these environments, individuals often feel more empowered to express themselves and explore their creativity freely, leading to more productive interactions. Have you considered local meet-ups, smaller online groups, or even one-on-one sessions where you can receive constructive feedback in a supportive atmosphere? How did you handle jam sessions?\",\"assistant\",[33]],[\"s66\",\"d8\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 86–88 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s67\",\"d8\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s68\",\"d8\",105,377,\"User: I just published a review on an album that beautifully merges Pacific sounds and electronic music. It showcases not only remarkable technical skill but also an emotional depth that resonates with listeners, drawing them into a journey through different soundscapes. \",\"user\",[86,87]],[\"s69\",\"d8\",377,679,\"The artists behind this project have brilliantly incorporated traditional instruments alongside contemporary production techniques, crafting a sound that feels both nostalgic and modern. I focused on how the album pays homage to its roots while also pushing boundaries that invite new interpretations. \",\"user\",[86,87]],[\"s70\",\"d8\",679,1078,\"This intersection of old and new has opened up a fascinating dialogue about the evolution of music and its role in cultural expression.\\n\\nUser: Attending a workshop recently helped me realize how important album reviews can be in shaping listener perspectives. Before this experience, I had never fully appreciated the weight that a well-articulated review could carry in influencing musical tastes. \",\"user\",[86,87]],[\"s71\",\"d8\",1078,1378,\"It was enlightening to see how reviews can provide context, allowing listeners to engage with an album on a deeper level beyond just the sound. This newfound understanding has transformed my view on their significance, opening up a pathway for me to explore music in ways I hadn't considered before. \",\"user\",[86,87]],[\"s72\",\"d8\",1378,1514,\"Now, I find myself analyzing reviews more closely, seeing them as a bridge between the artist's intention and the audience's experience.\",\"user\",[86,87]],[\"s73\",\"d8\",1514,1527,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s74\",\"d8\",1527,1924,\"Assistant: That's a great shift in mindset! It's truly fascinating how reviews act as a lens through which listeners can better understand and appreciate the intricate layers of music. They can highlight elements that may go unnoticed, such as the cultural significance of certain sounds or the technical prowess behind the production. Have you noticed any changes in your approach to podcasting? \",\"assistant\",[88]],[\"s75\",\"d8\",1924,2310,\"It must also be exciting to incorporate these reflections into your creative process, further enriching the discussions you present to your audience. Each episode can become a conversation starter, transforming how listeners interact with the music you discuss. The feedback you've received must have been rewarding, affirming your ability to connect with others through your insights. \",\"assistant\",[88]],[\"s76\",\"d8\",2310,2617,\"I'm sure your listeners appreciate this fresh perspective, as it fosters a deeper connection to the music and artists you feature. It's remarkable how a single workshop can ignite such substantial changes in one's creative journey, isn't it? I'm eager to see how this will influence your work going forward!\",\"assistant\",[88]],[\"s88\",\"d9\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 159–160 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s89\",\"d9\",101,107,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s90\",\"d9\",107,356,\"User: After several disagreements over the artistic direction, I felt stifled, which really discouraged me from that collaborative process. It was as if the creative vision I had in mind was at odds with the direction my bandmates wanted to pursue. \",\"user\",[159]],[\"s91\",\"d9\",356,713,\"I remember those discussions often being emotionally charged, where opinions clashed and passion ran high, but ultimately, it was clear that I couldn't contribute to something that did not resonate with my artistic essence. Feeling restricted in that environment made me question not just my contributions, but also my abilities and instincts as an artist. \",\"user\",[159]],[\"s92\",\"d9\",713,896,\"This inner turmoil prompted a desire for more autonomy over my own creative endeavors, leading to a pivotal decision to explore my artistry in a more personal and independent setting.\",\"user\",[159]],[\"s93\",\"d9\",896,909,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s94\",\"d9\",909,1168,\"Assistant: That sounds tough. It’s important to feel aligned with your collaborators. A collaborative effort should ideally enhance your creativity rather than hinder it, allowing every member to shine in their unique ways and share in the collective vision. \",\"assistant\",[160]],[\"s95\",\"d9\",1168,1486,\"When disagreements escalate, it can create a rift that not only affects the project but can also take a toll on personal relationships, leading to frustration and disillusionment. I'm glad to hear that you’re taking proactive steps toward something that feels right for you. What have you been focusing on since then? \",\"assistant\",[160]],[\"s96\",\"d9\",1486,1680,\"Redirecting your energy into new creative pursuits can be incredibly liberating, allowing you to thrive as an artist in your own right and explore territories you've always wanted to delve into.\",\"assistant\",[160]],[\"s97\",\"d10\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 43–44 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s98\",\"d10\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s99\",\"d10\",105,478,\"User: I left feeling unsatisfied, as though the film skimmed over the intricacies that make music a universal language. It was almost as if they focused too much on celebrity interviews and not enough on the artistic process itself. I found myself reflecting on how music has the power to unite diverse cultures and express emotions that words alone often fail to capture. \",\"user\",[43]],[\"s100\",\"d10\",478,845,\"The disappointment lingered as I thought about the many documentaries that delve into the creative journeys of musicians, revealing not just their triumphs but also their struggles and failures. It made me realize that true connection with music often comes from a deeper engagement, one that can be achieved through personal creation rather than passive consumption.\",\"user\",[43]],[\"s101\",\"d10\",845,858,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s102\",\"d10\",858,1223,\"Assistant: That’s an inspiring mindset! The journey of creating one's own music can be immensely fulfilling, as it allows for a deep personal expression that often transcends verbal communication. Have you tried composing original music? It can be an incredibly rewarding experience, as every note and lyric may reflect your thoughts and emotions in a genuine way. \",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s103\",\"d10\",1223,1407,\"Crafting melodies and harmonies also provides a unique outlet to process your own experiences and feelings; oftentimes, that raw authenticity resonates more than polished productions. \",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s104\",\"d10\",1407,1725,\"I understand that it can initially feel daunting, especially considering the plethora of skilled musicians out there, but remember that each artist started somewhere, often experimenting and learning through the process. It’s perfectly natural to encounter challenges, as the act of creation is rarely linear or easy. \",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s105\",\"d10\",1725,2062,\"Perhaps approaching it with a spirit of playfulness rather than obligation could rekindle that joy you're seeking. It's about discovering what resonates with you personally and allowing your creativity to flow. You might find that sometimes, the act of making music, irrespective of the final outcome, is what truly nurtures your spirit.\",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s106\",\"d11\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 40–42 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s107\",\"d11\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s108\",\"d11\",105,430,\"User: I explored audio production techniques, but it just didn’t resonate with me, and I found myself tangled in technical details rather than embracing the creativity. I realized that while understanding the mechanics of sound is important, my true passion seems to lie more in experiencing music rather than dissecting it. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s109\",\"d11\",430,749,\"Despite my attempts to immerse myself in the production process, I came to feel it was more of a chore and less of the rewarding experience I had initially anticipated. I think I am more drawn to the emotional aspects of music, like the storytelling elements in lyrics or the feelings evoked by melodies and harmonies. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s110\",\"d11\",749,1006,\"Perhaps, I should focus my energy on areas that allow me to connect with music on a more emotional level.\\n\\nUser: It genuinely feels much better to focus on what truly inspires me, such as creating my own tracks, which bring me immense joy and satisfaction. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s111\",\"d11\",1006,1339,\"This process of creation allows me to express emotions and ideas that words sometimes fail to capture, acting as an outlet for my inner thoughts and feelings. Additionally, I find that crafting my own music provides me with a sense of accomplishment and personal growth, which is invaluable in a world often filled with uncertainty. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s112\",\"d11\",1339,1686,\"Music has a way of resonating with my soul, and every track I create becomes a piece of my identity and a reflection of my experiences. In contrast, when I watched a music documentary, it felt like something was missing, as it didn’t engage me in the way I had hoped, failing to evoke that same deep connection I feel when I compose my own pieces.\",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s113\",\"d11\",1686,1699,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s114\",\"d11\",1699,2074,\"Assistant: I completely understand where you're coming from, as focusing on your personal inspirations can lead to much more fulfilling creative experiences. When you channel your energy into producing music that resonates with you, it sets the stage for a more meaningful artistic journey, one where every note and beat are imbued with your unique perspective and emotions. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s115\",\"d11\",2074,2413,\"The importance of self-expression through music cannot be overstated; it serves not only as a form of art but also as a therapeutic outlet. The reason documentaries can sometimes feel lacking is that they often offer an external perspective, stripping away the intimate connection that comes from creating something personally meaningful. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s116\",\"d11\",2413,2670,\"While documentaries can provide insights and inspiration, they may not have the same emotional weight as hearing your own creations come to life, as they can't replicate the enriching experience of your own artistic journey and how it unfolds in real time. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s117\",\"d11\",2670,2896,\"It's essential to honor that desire to create authentically, for it's in those moments of genuine expression that true artistry emerges, transforming mere sounds into something transcendent that can touch the hearts of others.\",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s118\",\"d12\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 37–39 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s119\",\"d12\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s120\",\"d12\",105,393,\"User: It was something I tried in 2020, but researching historical music trends felt tedious and uninspiring. Despite my initial enthusiasm, diving into the vast amounts of literature, videos, and academic papers often felt overwhelming, almost like searching for a needle in a haystack. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s121\",\"d12\",393,638,\"The more I tried to pinpoint what fascinated me, the more daunting it became, complicating the pursuit of enjoyable learning. Perhaps due to this overload of information, I lost sight of what initially drew me to the subject in the first place. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s122\",\"d12\",638,828,\"It made me realize that sometimes a less structured approach to exploration could be more fulfilling, allowing for genuine interest to emerge rather than adhering strictly to a curriculum.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[37,38]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past_to_current\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"history_evidence\",\"summary_revision_contracts\":{\"changes\":{\"previous_version\":1,\"eligible_route_ids\":[\"fact_7e68895df86673f7eac3f787\"],\"required_source_ids\":[\"s32\",\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s34\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s36\",\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s35\",\"s9\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\",\"s33\"]}},\"repair_scope\":{\"failed\":[{\"variable\":\"changes\",\"id\":\"*\",\"feedback\":\"Provider explicitly truncated reasoning output\",\"observation\":null,\"slot\":null}],\"attempt\":1,\"previous_response_identity\":\"82b0e6fd028c4391766070b586e48261c6e3753db9f985c80f7d6a0396e339f4\",\"invalid_response\":\"{\\n  \\\"slots\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"variable\\\": \\\"changes\\\",\\n      \\\"observations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"fact_7e68895df86673f7eac3f787\\\",\\n          \\\"stance\\\": \\\"support\\\",\\n          \\\"value\\\": \\\"The user's approach to music expression has shifted from public, analytical, and structured forms (such as writing reviews, podcasting, and formal album analysis) toward more personal, less public, and emotionally authentic ways of engaging with music. They have moved away from activities that felt pressured or template-driven—like reviewing albums objectively, running a time-consuming podcast, or dissecting music theory—and instead embraced sharing playlists, discussing music with friends, organizing a cultural festival, and enjoying music for its own sake without rigid guidelines. This change reflects a desire to preserve joy and emotional connection over external validation or analytical rigor.\\\",\\n          \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s32\\\", \\\"s8\\\", \\\"s22\\\", \\\"s34\\\", \\\"s23\\\", \\\"s45\\\", \\\"s44\\\", \\\"s36\\\", \\\"s24\\\", \\\"s3\\\", \\\"s35\\\", \\\"s9\\\", \\\"s7\\\", \\\"s21\\\", \\\"s20\\\", \\\"s4\\\", \\\"s33\\\"],\\n          \\\"entity_scope\\\": \\\"user\\\",\\n          \\\"time_scope\\\": \\\"past_to_current\\\",\\n          \\\"parent_versions\\\": {},\\n          \\\"retract_ids\\\": [],\\n          \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The user describes multiple shifts: from writing reviews that were criticized (s3, s4) to feeling that analytical reviewing drained joy (s7, s8, s44, s45); from a time-consuming podcast (s20, s21, s22, s23) to considering alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing with friends (s9); and from structured content creation to organizing a festival celebrating Pacific Islander artists (s32, s33, s34, s35, s36). The user also reflects on moving toward more personal, less public expression (s4) and rethinking how to share music authentically (s24). These sources collectively support a shift from public/analytical/structured to personal/emotional/community-oriented engagement.\\\",\\n          \\\"summary_revision\\\": {\\n            \\\"supersedes_route_ids\\\": [\\\"fact_7e68895df86673f7eac3f787\\\"],\\n            \\\"previous_version\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Re-reading all\"},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":