d examined by people who missed the nuance of their opinion. This pressure led them to second-guess their thoughts and emotional connection to the music. The joy of sharing their perspective on albums was overshadowed by fear of backlash. They also tried reviewing an album in 2019, but it felt unproductive and like forcing themselves to conform to a template that drained the fun. They attempted a podcast about music trends in 2018, but it became too time-consuming and felt like a chore, leading them to pause it. They lost interest in analytical music review halfway through, feeling it took away the joy of music. Overall, these experiences led them to realize their passion for music needed to be expressed in a more personal, less public way.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s3\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly describes being criticized for lack of objectivity, feeling under scrutiny, second-guessing, and joy being overshadowed by fear of backlash (s3, s4). They describe a 2019 review attempt that felt unproductive and like conforming to a template (s7, s8). They describe a 2018 podcast that became too time-consuming and felt like a chore (s20, s21, s22, s23). They describe losing interest in analytical review because it took away joy (s44, s45). These are all past experiences with writing music reviews or related analytical activities, supporting the complete summary.\",\"variable\":\"review_experience\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"},{\"id\":\"fact_ad6513cfe94cc7a10fecb1da\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user currently feels that the joy they once found in sharing their perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash, and that their passion for music needs to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, which they are finally starting to embrace. They have also real